  "description": "Alaska's widebody scheme, inspired by the aurora borealis: a white fuselage with the navy 'Alaska' wordmark large across the forward windows; a thin emerald band along the windows from ahead of the wing widens aft into a sweep of emerald, aqua-green and blue that rises to fill the aft fuselage, the blue reaching the crown at the fin; the fin blue to navy with two aqua-green ribbons, sharp-edged below and fading upward, running from the fillet up to the trailing edge; no Native face on the tail. White engines with an emerald swoosh along the top of each nacelle, widening aft. Worn by every Alaska 787-9.",
