  "notes": "Measured on N782HA (2026-04-23, left side, long lens, fitted to the 787-9 shape) for the aft sweep's edges and the title, and on Alaska's own press photos of N784HA (December 2025) for the fin's ribbons and the nacelle. The aurora is halftone gradients: drawn as flat fields, each fade cut at about its middle; the fin's two ribbons and the fuselage's aqua have sharp lower edges in paint, their upper edges are fades. The right side mirrors the left (N781HA, N783HA). Tagged by airframe in airframes/ASA.json because the jets fly as ASA and the callsign default (Alaska's 737 standard) would be wrong for them. The ex-Hawaiian registrations stay (N780HA-N784HA). Alaska's further 787-9 deliveries (through 2027) and the 787-10s (from 2028) will wear it: tag them as they arrive.",
  "history": "Announced 2025-08-04 with Alaska's first European routes; the first jet, N784HA (built for Hawaiian, delivered December 2025 in white and painted at Fort Worth), was shown at Boeing Field on 2026-01-07. Hawaiian's four 787-9s (N780HA-N783HA) traded their Pualani livery for it by spring 2026 (N780HA by October) as the 787s moved to Seattle."
